<title>TURKEY: Turk Isbank Q1 net up at 16.4 trln lira.</title>
<headline>Turk Isbank Q1 net up at 16.4 trln lira.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jan-March 1997 provisional</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>    Per share profit (lira)  1,640.02 vs     510.03</p>
<p>    Net profit		  16,400.15 vs   5,100.25</p>
<p>    Net interest income     27,662.49 vs  15,553.07</p>
<p>    Net non-interest expense 5,849.85 vs   6,602.82</p>
<p>    Provisions for bad loans   984.69 vs     464.37</p>
<p>    Loans			382,381.19 vs 171,677.00</p>
<p>    Deposits		   541,113.76 vs 271,520.43</p>
<p>    Loans borrowed	    66,612.47 vs  23,115.33</p>
<p>    Equity			81,187.97 vs  35,556.91</p>
<p>    Capital		     10,000.00 vs  10,000.00</p>
<p>NOTE - Turkiye Is Bankasi A.S. is one of Turkey's leading commercial banks.</p>
<p>It started to distribute a total 4.05 trillion lira cash dividend from 1996 profits on April 30.</p>
<p>The figures above do not take into account Turkey's 77 percent annual inflation in March.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-2750875.</p>
</text>
